{"@timestamp":"2026-10-09T22:29:35.6735134+05:30","@version":"1","message":"Exit: com.examly.springapp.service.ChatService.processChat() with result = ChatResponseDTO[reply=Based on your past feedback for *Clean Code*, the key concepts you value are books with a **\"complete in detail description\"** that are **\"easy to understand\"** and great for **\"beginners.\"** \n\nSince you appreciated the detailed yet accessible nature of your last programming read, here are a few highly recommended books from our collection that match those keywords:\n\n1. **The Pragmatic Programmer by Andrew Hunt (Genre: Programming)**\n   * **Why it fits:** This is a highly detailed, practical guide that breaks down software engineering best practices into easy-to-understand, actionable advice. It is widely considered a must-read for beginners and experienced developers alike who want a clear, comprehensive understanding of the craft.\n\n2. **Spring in Action by Craig Walls (Genre: Programming)**\n   * **Why it fits:** If you want another detailed, step-by-step guide, this book is perfect. It is known for taking complex concepts within the Spring Framework and explaining them in a hands-on, easy-to-follow manner with complete examples.\n\n3. **Thinking, Fast and Slow by Daniel Kahneman (Genre: Non-Fiction)**\n   * **Why it fits:** If you want to step outside of programming but keep the same style of reading, this book offers a complete, incredibly detailed, yet highly accessible breakdown of how the human mind works. \n\nTo rent any of these, just head to **Books > View Books** and click the green **Rent** button! Let me know if you need help with anything else., matched=true, matchedQuestion=null, category=null, confidence=1.0, source=gemini-ai, sessionId=session-3zt55n2, resolvedQuestion=based on my feedback recomend me more books and capture keywords from my olf feedback], Execution Time: 7901 ms","logger_name":"com.examly.springapp.aspect.LoggingAspect","thread_name":"http-nio-8080-e